{# Deployed content (/etc/modprobe.d/zfs-arc.conf), and the writing task
   notifies `Rebuild initramfs for zfs arc cap`. A comment reword here costs
   every existing consumer an initramfs rebuild per host on its next converge,
   so keep this byte-stable and put narrative in README.md. #}
# {{ ansible_managed }}
# Managed by the zfs_arc_cap Ansible role (compute Proxmox hosts).
#
# zfs_arc_max caps the ZFS ARC in bytes. It is a LOAD-TIME module parameter, so
# it only takes effect at the value present when the zfs module loads — which on
# these hosts is during the initramfs (the local-ssd pool imports at early boot).
# The role therefore rebuilds the initramfs whenever this file changes, and also
# writes the running value to /sys/module/zfs/parameters/zfs_arc_max so a changed
# cap applies live without a reboot. Value comes from zfs_arc_cap_max_bytes.
options zfs zfs_arc_max={{ zfs_arc_cap_max_bytes }}
